{"title":"Technical Artist — Career Roadmap","role":"Technical Artist","summary":"Career focus: A Technical Artist (TA) bridges art and technology in game development. The role involves making game art work efficiently inside a real-time engine by solving problems involving shaders, materials, rendering, pipelines, optimization, tools, procedural workflows and artist–programmer collaboration.","facts":{"Current degree":"B.Des (Bachelor of Design)","Course":"Game Design / Games Art"},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Career Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A Technical Artist ensures that high-quality game assets can be created, integrated, rendered and optimized efficiently."},{"type":"h","text":"Typical Responsibilities"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Develop and maintain art pipelines"},{"text":"Create shaders and materials"},{"text":"Optimize 3D assets"},{"text":"Build artist-facing tools"},{"text":"Work with Unreal Engine / Unity"},{"text":"Configure lighting and rendering"},{"text":"Develop procedural workflows"},{"text":"Solve technical problems for artists"},{"text":"Optimize textures, meshes and draw calls"},{"text":"Support VFX and animation pipelines"},{"text":"Integrate assets into game engines"},{"text":"Collaborate with programmers, artists and designers"},{"text":"Establish technical art standards"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Core Position"},{"type":"flow","items":["Artist","Technical Problem Solver","Game Engine Specialist"],"sep":"+"}]},{"heading":"Career Horizons — 2026–2046","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Period","Career Development"],"rows":[[{"text":"2026–2028"},{"text":"Design foundation + 3D + programming fundamentals"}],[{"text":"2028–2030"},{"text":"Game/technical art internship + junior TA role"}],[{"text":"2030–2033"},{"text":"Technical Artist"}],[{"text":"2033–2037"},{"text":"Senior Technical Artist"}],[{"text":"2037–2040"},{"text":"Lead Technical Artist"}],[{"text":"2040